  60: ## 2. Decisions
  61: 
  62: ### D-A â€” "Verified" is Supabase Auth's own fact. No migration, no new column.
  63: The observable behind AT-001.09 is `email_confirmed_at` on the auth user â€” GoTrue's field, set
  64: by GoTrue when the emailed link is used. Nothing this leaf ships writes it, `public.accounts`
  65: gains no column, and this item ships **no migration**. Consequence: there is no schema, RLS or
  66: privilege surface to prove here; the live proof reads `auth.users.email_confirmed_at` as
  67: operator evidence only.
  68: 
  69: ### D-B â€” The config flip, and one pre-authorized relief valve
  70: `[auth.email] enable_confirmations` flips to `true` in `supabase/config.toml` â€” the change the
  71: b-file header explicitly reserves for this leaf. The comment beside it is updated to say what it
  72: changes and which leaf owns it. **Pre-authorized amendment:** if step 5's registrations starve
  73: on the 2-per-hour `[auth.rate_limit] email_sent` limit (429 or absent mail), the executor raises
  74: that value (e.g. to 100) in the same file, restarts the stack, and records the raise in the
  75: transcript. This is local-stack configuration; no hosted deployment exists.
  76: 
  77: ### D-C â€” The gate is a shipped decision module: `supabase/functions/_shared/verification.ts`
  78: A new module under the same two constraints as `accounts.ts` (relative imports only, no Deno
  79: global, no I/O; its type coverage is its import from the acceptance program). Two exports:
  80: 
  81: - `emailVerifiedFromUser(user: unknown): boolean` â€” judges the GoTrue `/auth/v1/user` response
  82:   shape: a non-empty string `email_confirmed_at` means verified; **anything else â€” missing
  83:   field, null, non-string, malformed object â€” means unverified.** Fail closed.
  84: - `discoveryMessageAllowed(caller: { emailVerified: boolean }): Decision<'verified'>` â€”
  85:   `Decision` imported from `./accounts.ts`. The ONLY allow is `caller?.emailVerified === true`;
  86:   a missing or malformed caller argument refuses (the same fail-closed posture, for the same
  87:   measured reason: edge entry points have no type-checker). The refusal reason names email
  88:   verification as what is missing AND as the remedy, in words AT-001.10's assertion can match.
  89: 
  90: The gate is **type-blind**: decision-8 makes verification the floor for ANY Discovery message.
  91: AT-001.10's unverified-NGO subject is an instance of that rule, not its scope, and a gate that
  92: read the account type would be shipping a distinction no ratified text draws.
  93: 
  94: Why a new module rather than growing `accounts.ts`: that file's header scopes it to the account
  95: deliverable's decisions; `github.ts` already set the several-small-modules precedent; and this
  96: rule's future caller is the Discovery send route, not signup.
  97: 
  98: ### D-D â€” No Discovery surface ships. The gate is the hook the route must call.
  99: The Discovery message route belongs to REQ-002/004 (the migration doc maps it to a future
 100: `discovery-message` edge function). Building an edge function or a table for it here would be
 101: another requirement's surface invented early. What this leaf ships is the **decision** that
 102: route must consult â€” exactly the pattern the suite already ratifies for
 103: `hasPlatformAcknowledgment` ("this is the hook the leaf that lands project creation must call").
 104: The module header and section 4 both state it plainly: **the gate has no deployed caller yet**,
 105: and no green from this item may be read as "Discovery messaging is gated in production."
 106: 
 107: At the loop tier the SUT gains a `sendDiscoveryMessage` operation and the fixture is the
 108: stand-in surface: it renders the caller's GoTrue user shape from stored Auth state, derives the
 109: verified fact through the SHIPPED `emailVerifiedFromUser`, consults the SHIPPED
 110: `discoveryMessageAllowed`, refuses with the gate's own reason and **writes nothing**, or on
 111: allow records the message in fixture storage. Every judgement is the shipped module's; the
 112: storage is a Map like all the rest.
 113: 
 114: ### D-E â€” Fixture and contract: mirror Auth's verification state, judge nothing
 115: `_fixture.ts`: `AuthUser` gains `emailConfirmedAt: string | null` and
 116: `verificationLink: string | null`. An email/password registration starts unconfirmed and mints
 117: a link value (the fixture's stand-in for the emailed link the mail catcher would hold). A
 118: provider registration (Google/GitHub) starts confirmed â€” the expected GoTrue behaviour when the
 119: provider vouches for the address. **This mirror is UNBOUND by this item** (gate-1 ruling [1],
 120: section 7): no OAuth app or credential exists in this environment, so no live provider session
 121: is obtainable â€” the same recorded gap that leaves the OAuth handshake itself unproved at every
